<article class="env-definition" id="048N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/048N">Definition <span data-tag="048N">83.5.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme, and let $B$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $j : R \to U \times _ B U$ be a pre-relation over $B$. If $u \in |U|$, then the <em>orbit</em>, or more precisely the <em>$R$-orbit</em> of $u$ is </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  O_ u = \left\{  u' \in |U|\  : \begin{matrix}  \exists n \geq 1, \  \exists u_0, \ldots , u_ n \in |U|\text{ such that } u_0 = u \text{ and } u_ n = u' 

\\  \text{and for all }i \in \{ 0, \ldots , n - 1\} \text{ either } u_ i = u_{i + 1}\text{ or } 

\\  \exists r \in |R|, \  s(r) = u_ i, t(r) = u_{i + 1} \text{ or } 

\\  \exists r \in |R|, \  t(r) = u_ i, s(r) = u_{i + 1} 

\end{matrix} \right\}   \]
</div>
</article>